Title: Resume Scanner

Objective: Build a web tool to:
- Select a Job Description (JD) from stored .md files in documents/JD and display the list for user selection.
- Upload a candidate resume (PDF).
- Use LangGraph to coordinate OPENAI GPT agents to analyze the match between the selected JD and uploaded resume.
- If the match score is >75%, automatically generate a set of interview questions for the applicant (as described in project.md) using OPENAI GPT API.
- Use Pinecone to store the resume and JD embeddings.
- Use Tesseract OCR to extract text from .pdf files that contains images and return the text -> save the text to .txt file in a separated folder -> embed the text using OpenAI API -> store the embeddings in Pinecone.
- Create a sidebar to manage sessions so that an evaluation of a resume is stored along with its matching score & questions
   -> user can revisit later (similar to how session works in ChatGPT)
   -> user can rename/ delete a session by click on the 3 dots on the right side of its name
- Create a button "Add JD" -> spawn a modal to let user add more JDs by uploading a .txt/.md file -> All JDs will be stored in documents/JD folder

Core_Features:
- JD_Selection: List and select .md files from documents/JD.
- Resume_Upload: Upload resume in PDF format.
- LangGraph_Orchestration: Use LangGraph to coordinate OPENAI GPT agents for resume-JD matching.
- Scoring: Calculate match score (percentage).
- Auto_Questionnaire: If score >75%, generate tailored questionnaire using OPENAI GPT API, the questionnaire can be interactively refined by the user (defined in interactive.prp), latest version of the questionnaire will be stored in the session.
- Reporting: Display match score, missing skills, and generated questions.
- Add_JD: Add new JD by uploading a .txt/.md file -> All JDs will be stored in documents/JD folder

Technical_Stack:
- Language: Python
- Libraries:
  - PDF_Parsing: pdfplumber
  - DOCX_Parsing: python-docx
  - NLP: spaCy or NLTK
- Coordinating Agents: LangGraph
- Vector DB: Pinecone
- OCR: Tesseract
- Web_Framework: streamlit for the user interface.

UI:
- A web-based interface for uploading files/pasting text and viewing the analysis report, with sessions management sidebar similar to how ChatGPT works, where history of sessions are stored and can be revisited.

Core-rules:
- Use `uv add` command to install packages not `pip install`
- Later on if you want to run python script, use `uv run python main.py`
- Retrieve configurations from .streamlit/secrets.toml instead of .env
- Never delete or alter any rows in .streamlit/secrets.toml because it is used for the functionality of the application.
- Never delete or alter any rows in .env because it is used for the functionality of GEMINI agents.